# Database & Drizzle Guidelines

Best practices for database design and Drizzle ORM usage with SQLite.

## Schema Design Principles

### General Rules
- **Use UUIDs for primary keys** — avoid auto-increment for distributed-friendly design
- **Always include timestamps** — `createdAt` and `updatedAt` on every table
- **Use soft deletes sparingly** — only when audit trail is required
- **Normalize appropriately** — don't over-normalize, denormalize for read performance where justified
- **Name tables in plural** — `users`, `tickets`, `comments`
- **Name columns in camelCase** — Drizzle maps to snake_case automatically if configured

### SQLite-Specific Considerations
- **No native UUID type** — use `text` for UUIDs
- **No native boolean** — use `integer` (0/1)
- **No native datetime** — use `integer` (Unix timestamp) or `text` (ISO string)
- **Limited ALTER TABLE** — plan schema carefully, migrations can be painful
- **Single writer** — design for sequential writes, concurrent reads

## Drizzle Schema Conventions

### Table Definition
```typescript
// packages/shared/src/schemas/ticket.ts
import { sqliteTable, text, integer } from 'drizzle-orm/sqlite-core';
import { createInsertSchema, createSelectSchema } from 'drizzle-zod';
import { z } from 'zod';

// Constants
export const TICKET_STATUS = ['backlog', 'todo', 'in_progress', 'review', 'done'] as const;
export const TICKET_PRIORITY = ['low', 'medium', 'high', 'critical'] as const;

// Table definition
export const tickets = sqliteTable('tickets', {
  // Primary key
  id: text('id').primaryKey(), // UUID stored as text
  
  // Foreign keys
  projectId: text('project_id')
    .notNull()
    .references(() => projects.id, { onDelete: 'cascade' }),
  assigneeId: text('assignee_id')
    .references(() => users.id, { onDelete: 'set null' }),
  reporterId: text('reporter_id')
    .notNull()
    .references(() => users.id, { onDelete: 'restrict' }),
  
  // Business fields
  number: integer('number').notNull(), // Per-project ticket number
  title: text('title').notNull(),
  description: text('description'),
  status: text('status', { enum: TICKET_STATUS }).notNull().default('backlog'),
  priority: text('priority', { enum: TICKET_PRIORITY }).notNull().default('medium'),
  
  // Timestamps (stored as Unix milliseconds)
  createdAt: integer('created_at', { mode: 'timestamp_ms' }).notNull(),
  updatedAt: integer('updated_at', { mode: 'timestamp_ms' }).notNull(),
});

// Zod schemas (generated from Drizzle schema)
export const insertTicketSchema = createInsertSchema(tickets, {
  // Override/refine validations
  title: z.string().min(1).max(255),
  description: z.string().max(10000).optional(),
});

export const selectTicketSchema = createSelectSchema(tickets);

// Types inferred from schemas
export type Ticket = z.infer<typeof selectTicketSchema>;
export type InsertTicket = z.infer<typeof insertTicketSchema>;
```

### Relations Definition
```typescript
// packages/shared/src/schemas/relations.ts
import { relations } from 'drizzle-orm';
import { users, projects, tickets, comments } from './index';

export const usersRelations = relations(users, ({ many }) => ({
  assignedTickets: many(tickets, { relationName: 'assignee' }),
  reportedTickets: many(tickets, { relationName: 'reporter' }),
  comments: many(comments),
  projects: many(projects),
}));

export const projectsRelations = relations(projects, ({ one, many }) => ({
  createdBy: one(users, {
    fields: [projects.createdById],
    references: [users.id],
  }),
  tickets: many(tickets),
}));

export const ticketsRelations = relations(tickets, ({ one, many }) => ({
  project: one(projects, {
    fields: [tickets.projectId],
    references: [projects.id],
  }),
  assignee: one(users, {
    fields: [tickets.assigneeId],
    references: [users.id],
    relationName: 'assignee',
  }),
  reporter: one(users, {
    fields: [tickets.reporterId],
    references: [users.id],
    relationName: 'reporter',
  }),
  comments: many(comments),
}));

export const commentsRelations = relations(comments, ({ one }) => ({
  ticket: one(tickets, {
    fields: [comments.ticketId],
    references: [tickets.id],
  }),
  author: one(users, {
    fields: [comments.authorId],
    references: [users.id],
  }),
}));
```

### Index Definition
```typescript
import { sqliteTable, text, integer, index, uniqueIndex } from 'drizzle-orm/sqlite-core';

export const tickets = sqliteTable('tickets', {
  id: text('id').primaryKey(),
  projectId: text('project_id').notNull(),
  number: integer('number').notNull(),
  status: text('status').notNull(),
  assigneeId: text('assignee_id'),
  createdAt: integer('created_at', { mode: 'timestamp_ms' }).notNull(),
}, (table) => ({
  // Composite unique: ticket number is unique within a project
  projectNumberIdx: uniqueIndex('tickets_project_number_idx')
    .on(table.projectId, table.number),
  
  // Query optimization indexes
  projectStatusIdx: index('tickets_project_status_idx')
    .on(table.projectId, table.status),
  assigneeIdx: index('tickets_assignee_idx')
    .on(table.assigneeId),
  createdAtIdx: index('tickets_created_at_idx')
    .on(table.createdAt),
}));
```

## Query Patterns

### Basic CRUD
```typescript
import { eq, and, desc, sql } from 'drizzle-orm';

// Select one
const ticket = await db
  .select()
  .from(tickets)
  .where(eq(tickets.id, id))
  .limit(1)
  .then(rows => rows[0] ?? null);

// Select with conditions
const openTickets = await db
  .select()
  .from(tickets)
  .where(
    and(
      eq(tickets.projectId, projectId),
      eq(tickets.status, 'in_progress'),
    )
  )
  .orderBy(desc(tickets.createdAt));

// Insert
const [newTicket] = await db
  .insert(tickets)
  .values({
    id: crypto.randomUUID(),
    projectId,
    title,
    createdAt: new Date(),
    updatedAt: new Date(),
  })
  .returning();

// Update
const [updated] = await db
  .update(tickets)
  .set({ 
    status: 'done',
    updatedAt: new Date(),
  })
  .where(eq(tickets.id, id))
  .returning();

// Delete
await db
  .delete(tickets)
  .where(eq(tickets.id, id));
```

### Joins and Relations
```typescript
// Using Drizzle relations (recommended)
const ticketWithRelations = await db.query.tickets.findFirst({
  where: eq(tickets.id, id),
  with: {
    project: true,
    assignee: true,
    reporter: true,
    comments: {
      with: { author: true },
      orderBy: [desc(comments.createdAt)],
    },
  },
});

// Manual join when you need specific columns
const ticketsWithAssignee = await db
  .select({
    ticket: tickets,
    assigneeName: users.displayName,
  })
  .from(tickets)
  .leftJoin(users, eq(tickets.assigneeId, users.id))
  .where(eq(tickets.projectId, projectId));
```

### Pagination
```typescript
interface PaginationParams {
  page: number;  // 1-indexed
  pageSize: number;
}

async function getTicketsPaginated(
  projectId: string,
  { page, pageSize }: PaginationParams,
) {
  const offset = (page - 1) * pageSize;

  const [items, countResult] = await Promise.all([
    db
      .select()
      .from(tickets)
      .where(eq(tickets.projectId, projectId))
      .orderBy(desc(tickets.createdAt))
      .limit(pageSize)
      .offset(offset),
    db
      .select({ count: sql<number>`count(*)` })
      .from(tickets)
      .where(eq(tickets.projectId, projectId)),
  ]);

  const total = countResult[0]?.count ?? 0;

  return {
    items,
    pagination: {
      page,
      pageSize,
      total,
      totalPages: Math.ceil(total / pageSize),
    },
  };
}
```

### Transactions
```typescript
// Use transactions for operations that must be atomic
async function createTicket(projectId: string, data: CreateTicketDto) {
  return db.transaction(async (tx) => {
    // Get next ticket number (must be in transaction to avoid race)
    const [{ maxNumber }] = await tx
      .select({ maxNumber: sql<number>`COALESCE(MAX(${tickets.number}), 0)` })
      .from(tickets)
      .where(eq(tickets.projectId, projectId));

    // Create ticket with the next number
    const [ticket] = await tx
      .insert(tickets)
      .values({
        id: crypto.randomUUID(),
        projectId,
        number: maxNumber + 1,
        ...data,
        createdAt: new Date(),
        updatedAt: new Date(),
      })
      .returning();

    return ticket;
  });
}
```

## Migrations

### Migration File Structure
```
packages/server/src/database/
├── migrations/
│   ├── 0001_initial.sql
│   ├── 0002_add_ticket_priority.sql
│   └── meta/
│       └── _journal.json
├── migrate.ts
└── schema.ts
```

### Creating Migrations
```bash
# Generate migration from schema changes
pnpm drizzle-kit generate:sqlite

# Apply migrations
pnpm drizzle-kit push:sqlite  # Dev (direct push)
pnpm tsx src/database/migrate.ts  # Production (programmatic)
```

### Migration Script
```typescript
// packages/server/src/database/migrate.ts
import { migrate } from 'drizzle-orm/better-sqlite3/migrator';
import { drizzle } from 'drizzle-orm/better-sqlite3';
import Database from 'better-sqlite3';

const sqlite = new Database(process.env.DATABASE_PATH ?? './data/jirakli.db');
const db = drizzle(sqlite);

migrate(db, { migrationsFolder: './src/database/migrations' });

console.log('Migrations complete');
sqlite.close();
```

### Migration Best Practices
- **Never edit existing migrations** — create new ones
- **Test migrations on copy of production data** before deploying
- **Make migrations reversible** when possible
- **Keep migrations small and focused** — one change per migration
- **Include data migrations** when schema changes require it

## Performance Guidelines

### Indexing Strategy
- **Index foreign keys** — always
- **Index columns used in WHERE** — for frequent queries
- **Index columns used in ORDER BY** — if sorting large datasets
- **Use composite indexes** — for queries filtering on multiple columns
- **Don't over-index** — each index slows writes

### Query Optimization
```typescript
// Bad: N+1 query
const tickets = await db.select().from(tickets);
for (const ticket of tickets) {
  ticket.comments = await db
    .select()
    .from(comments)
    .where(eq(comments.ticketId, ticket.id));
}

// Good: Single query with relation
const tickets = await db.query.tickets.findMany({
  with: { comments: true },
});

// Good: Manual join if you need control
const tickets = await db
  .select()
  .from(tickets)
  .leftJoin(comments, eq(tickets.id, comments.ticketId));
```

### SQLite-Specific Optimizations
```typescript
// Enable WAL mode for better concurrency (do once at startup)
sqlite.pragma('journal_mode = WAL');

// Enable foreign keys (SQLite has them off by default)
sqlite.pragma('foreign_keys = ON');

// Optimize for read-heavy workloads
sqlite.pragma('synchronous = NORMAL');
sqlite.pragma('cache_size = -64000'); // 64MB cache
```

## Data Integrity

### Constraints
```typescript
export const tickets = sqliteTable('tickets', {
  // NOT NULL for required fields
  title: text('title').notNull(),
  
  // UNIQUE for natural keys
  // (handled via uniqueIndex for composite)
  
  // FOREIGN KEY with appropriate action
  projectId: text('project_id')
    .notNull()
    .references(() => projects.id, { onDelete: 'cascade' }),
  
  // CHECK constraints (via Zod at app layer, SQLite supports but Drizzle doesn't expose)
});
```

### Application-Level Validation
```typescript
// Validate with Zod before insert
const validated = insertTicketSchema.parse(input);
await db.insert(tickets).values(validated);
```

## Don'ts

- **Don't use raw SQL unless necessary** — Drizzle's type safety is valuable
- **Don't store large blobs** — SQLite handles them but it's not ideal
- **Don't ignore migrations in production** — always use proper migration flow
- **Don't use ORM for complex analytics** — consider raw SQL or separate read model
- **Don't trust client-provided IDs** — always generate UUIDs server-side
- **Don't skip transactions** for multi-step operations
